From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pyo <pyo@localhost>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 16:19:56 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat: delete old backups after a number of days

Backups are never deleted, so the bucket grows forever unless a
lifecycle rule removes old objects, which can also remove a backup a
restore still needs.  Add BackupPolicy spec.retentionDays (moco-backup
backup --retention-days).  After each successful backup, the backups
that no restore to a time within that many days needs are deleted:
those older than the newest backup taken at or before the cutoff.
0, the default, keeps every backup, as before.

A failure to delete is logged and does not fail the backup Job.
Bucket gets a Delete method for this.
